        },
        "text_bQNtcM": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Tooth enamel is the hardest substance in the human body, composed primarily of a mineral called hydroxyapatite. Although durable, enamel faces constant exposure to acids from foods, drinks, and plaque, which can gradually wear it down—especially since enamel doesn’t regenerate naturally. <br/>Our toothpaste features nano-hydroxyapatite (n-Ha), a fluoride alternative and biomimetic mineral. n-Ha is inspired by nature and backed by decades of scientific research.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        },
        "button_yQ4qYP": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
